# ── 4.2 Real-Time Socket Events ──────────────────────────────
# (Connect to ws://localhost:5000 with socket.io-client)
# After connecting, emit:  { event: "authenticate", data: { userId, role, driverId } }
#
# Events you will receive:
#   new_ride_request     → driver socket when rider creates request
#   bid_placed           → rider socket when driver submits bid
#   bid_accepted         → driver socket when rider accepts bid
#   driver_assigned      → rider socket when bid accepted (biddingController)
#   driver_assigned      → rider socket when fixed-price ride accepted (rideController)
#   ride_started         → rider socket
#   stop_arrived         → rider socket
#   stop_departed        → rider socket
#   ride_completed       → rider + driver sockets
#   ride_cancelled       → rider + driver sockets
#   ride_request_expired → rider socket (from worker, every 60s)
#   driver_en_route      → rider socket (every location update during active ride)

# 42. ✅ 🔑 Submit Bid (triggers bid_placed → rider socket)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bidding/requests/{{rideRequestId}}/submit
Authorization: {{driverToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bidAmount": 350,
  "estimatedArrivalMinutes": 5,
  "driverMessage": "On my way!"
}

###

# 43. ✅ 🔑 Accept Bid (triggers bid_accepted → driver socket, driver_assigned → rider socket)
